@startuml m3-sequence
title Member 3: Customer Books a Parcel (customer-order-service, port 8082)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 360
skinparam ParticipantPadding 14
autonumber

actor Customer
participant "Booking page\n(React)" as UI
participant "API Gateway\n(8080)" as GW
participant "Order Service\n(8082)" as OS
participant "Pricing Service\n(8083)" as PS
database "Order Database\n(swiftdrop_order)" as DB
queue "RabbitMQ\n(swiftdrop.events.exchange)" as MQ
participant "Dispatch\nService" as DS
participant "Webhook\nService" as WS
participant "Notification\nService" as NS

== Part 1: Fill in the form and see the fee ==

Customer -> UI : Fill in pickup, drop-off and parcel details\n(names, backup phones, address parts, size, weight, speed, notes)
UI -> UI : Check each step (required fields, phone format, postal code)
alt a step has mistakes
  UI --> Customer : Show the errors next to the fields
end
UI -> GW : POST /api/v1/orders/estimate (login token)
GW -> GW : Check the token and the customer role
alt not logged in / wrong role
  GW --> UI : 401 / 403
end
GW -> OS : Pass the request on (X-User-Id, X-User-Role, X-Correlation-Id)
OS -> OS : Check and clean the input again
alt input is invalid
  OS --> UI : 400 "Please check the highlighted fields"\n(no personal details in the message)
end
OS -> PS : POST /api/v1/pricing/quote\n(districts, weight, size, speed)
alt pricing works
  PS --> OS : Fee, breakdown and rule version (LKR)
  OS --> UI : Estimated fee and breakdown
  UI --> Customer : Show the fee before confirming
else pricing is down or too slow
  OS --> UI : 503 "Pricing service is temporarily unavailable"
  UI --> Customer : Show the message, Confirm stays off
end

== Part 2: Confirm the booking ==

Customer -> UI : Tick the prohibited-items declaration, click "Confirm and book"
UI -> GW : POST /api/v1/orders
GW -> OS : Pass the request on (customer id from the token)
OS -> OS : Check and clean the input
OS -> PS : Get the fee again (the price from the browser is never trusted)
PS --> OS : Final fee
OS -> OS : Make a tracking number (SD-XXXX-XXXX, not in sequence)
OS -> DB : Save the parcel in customer_orders (status CREATED)\nand add the first status history row
DB --> OS : Saved
OS ->> MQ : order.created\n(tracking number, districts, speed, fee; no addresses or phones)
OS ->> MQ : parcel.status.changed (CREATED)
OS --> UI : 200 OK (tracking number, fee)
UI --> Customer : Show "Parcel booked", the tracking number,\nlabel and receipt download, Track parcel

== Part 3: Other services react on their own ==

par order.created
  MQ ->> DS : dispatch.order-created.queue
  DS -> DS : Add to the list of parcels waiting for a courier
else order.created
  MQ ->> WS : webhook.events.queue
  WS -> WS : Send it to the webhook endpoints that subscribe to it
else parcel.status.changed
  MQ ->> NS : notification.events.queue
  NS -> NS : Send the customer a "parcel booked" SMS
end
note over MQ, NS
  The Real-Time Tracking Hub in the gateway also listens to
  parcel.status.changed, so the public tracking page starts at CREATED.
end note

== Part 4: Download the label and receipt ==

Customer -> UI : Click "Download label and receipt"
UI -> GW : GET /api/v1/orders/{id}/shipping-label (login token)
GW -> OS : Pass the request on
OS -> DB : Load the parcel
DB --> OS : Parcel
alt the parcel belongs to this customer
  OS -> OS : Make the 2-page PDF in memory\n(shipping label, then booking receipt; no file saved)
  OS --> UI : PDF file (receipt-<tracking number>.pdf)
  UI --> Customer : Label and receipt download
else the parcel belongs to someone else
  OS --> UI : 404 Not found (does not reveal the parcel exists)
end

@enduml
